  "worked_solution": "First, we find ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ and $\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{\u2032}(t) & =\u27e8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{3}({t}^{2}+2)^{3/2})\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e81,\\,t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2}\u27e9 \\\\ \u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(t\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+{t}^{2}({t}^{2}+2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({t}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the arc length of the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}({t}^{2}+1)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+t){|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}+2)-(\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3}+(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}+2+\\frac{1}{3}+1 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
